From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:40:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/51] port: run_id-tagged control block, pristine-log attach
 check, closed-run reinit

- Harness passes the same 64-bit run id to both nodes (MEGALON_RUN_ID or
  config run_id; required, low 32 bits non-zero). It replaces
  init_epoch_ns in the control block and is written before READY.
- Node 1 waits for state==READY && run_id==expected (a stale READY of
  another run is never attached to) and re-checks run id and READY in
  Finish, at the start barrier and after it.
- node_alive[i] holds the low 32 bits of run_id instead of 1.
- ffi nr_log_counters: read-only snapshot of head/tail/ltails; node 1
  refuses to attach unless all are 0 (gcd_nr.cc).
- Node 0 may re-initialize without the reinit flag only when the previous
  run closed cleanly (state CLOSED, no node alive); EMPTY still means an
  all-zero control page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
